# Why does this file exist? BuildKit reads a <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile in place of the root
# .dockerignore. The root one is the host image's allowlist (`*`, then the few files that image copies), which hid
# crimson_noir_os/Cargo.toml, crates/, boot/ and build.rs from this image's prefetch of the crates: the first real
# self-heal run stopped there ("build.rs: not found"). This file keeps only the build output, the installed modules
# and the repository's history out of the context (15 MB without them; gigabytes with).
# What breaks if it is removed? The sandbox image cannot be built, and the agent never reaches a failure.
.git
node_modules
crimson_noir_os/target
native/*/target
dist
dist-ssr
dist-pilot
**/__pycache__
# A developer's local AI tooling, at any depth, whatever an allowlist line above admits (tools/selfheal/sandbox.mjs AI_TOOLING)
**/.claude
**/.cursor
**/.continue
**/.codeium
**/.windsurf
**/.aider.conf.yml
**/.aider.chat.history.md
**/.aider.input.history
**/.aider.tags.cache.v3
**/.mcp.json
**/CLAUDE.local.md
